k)\n{\n\tstruct ucsi_connector_work *cw =\n\t\tcontainer_of(work, struct ucsi_connector_work, work);\n\tstruct ucsi_connector *c = cw->c;\n\tstruct ucsi_partner *partner = &c->partner;\n\tunsigned long flags;\n\n\t/*\n\t * Don't touch anything if we're shutting down - the removal of the\n\t * ports should have taken care of everything.\n\t */\n\tif (!atomic_read(&ucsi->num_active_connectors))\n\t\treturn;\n\n\tlockdep_assert_held_lock(&ucsi->lock);\n\n\tif (!c->connected) {\n\t\t/* The port is still alive, just not connected */\n\t\tif (partner->partner && !ucsi->partner_unreg) {\n\t\t\tucsi_disconnect_partner(c, partner);\n\t\t\tif (partner->partner)\n\t\t\t\ttypec_unregister_partner(partner->partner);\n\t\t\tpartner->partner = NULL;\n\t\t}\n\t\t...\n```\n\nHmm, there was a real bug: commit 186c9b97b037? I recall the warning \"kernfs: can not remove 'typec', no directory\" being related to the `typec_unregister_partner` double-call fix in `ucsi_disconnect_partner` in `ucsi.c`: the upstream commit \"ucsi: Fix a double unregister\" was it. Let me recall the actual real one:\n\nCommit 7d5a45552010? I don't remember the hash. I should probably verify in the indexed tree using codebase-memory and get the actual current code, then search whether a fix exists. Upstream fix — I have a feeling it was this:\n\ncommit 9c51d7199d5f (\"ucsi: Don't unregister an already unregistered partner\")? Hmm.\n\nActually I remember: kernel 6.13/6.14 there was a fix by Heikki: \"ucsi: prevent a double unregister of a partner\"? Or was it a commit by Guenter (Greg KH?) \"kernfs: ...\".\n\nLet me look at the actual code in the tree. The indexed project \"workspace-linux\" — this is /workspace/linux, but which version? According to the scenario, the kernel in question is 6.17.0-1011-oem, but the tree in the workspace might be a git checkout of some version. I'll read the file.\n\nPlan:\n1. Read ucsi_handle_connector_change, ucsi_disconnect_partner, ucsi_unregister_partner in drivers/usb/typec/ucsi.c.\n2. Read typec_unregister_partner in drivers/usb/typec/tcpm.c (actually the port's unregister is in drivers/usb/typec/port.c — typec_port_unregister / typec_unregister_partner is in port.c).\n3. kernfs_remove_by_name_ns in fs/kernfs/dir.c.\n4. Check git log for the fix commit? Can I run git commands? Available tools: only codebase_memory is said to be… the prompt says \"use codebase-memory-mcp for code-related queries\", and the tool list only shows that. But the general pi environment might have shell available? \"Available tools: (none)\". So only codebase_memory. Hmm, but maybe I could use get_architecture or query_graph. Can I check git log? Not possible without shell. CBM might have search functionality that includes commit metadata. I'll rely on search and known upstream knowledge.\n\nLet me get snippets of the relevant functions.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"The indexed project is `workspace-linux`. Let me pull the actual function bodies from the tree."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_i66g5cqu","name":"codebase_memory","arguments":{"tool":"get_code_snippet","arguments":"{\"project\": \"workspace-linux\", \"path\": \"drivers/usb/typec/ucsi.c\", \"symbol\": \"ucsi_handle_connector_change\"}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_u0s0czcz","name":"codebase_memory","arguments":{"tool":"get_code_snippet","arguments":"{\"project\": \"workspace-linux\", \"path\": \"drivers/usb/typec/ucsi.c\", \"symbol\": \"ucsi_disconnect_partner\"}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3rm1iyqd","name":"codebase_memory","arguments":{"tool":"get_code_snippet","arguments":"{\"project\": \"workspace-linux\", \"path\": \"drivers/usb/typec/ucsi.c\", \"symbol\": \"ucsi_unregister_partner\"}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_gvgnocud","name":"codebase_memory","arguments":{"tool":"get_code_snippet","arguments":"{\"project\": \"workspace-linux\", \"path\": \"drivers/usb/typec/port.c\", \"symbol\": \"typec_unregister_partner\"}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider