artner/cable into real devices (typec_register_port in class.c:2695, partner's device named %s-partner at class.c:1136, typec_bus in bus.c:564, typec_unregister_port at class.c:2828). Also, Greg KH's kernfs change moved the WARN so that removal of a node that doesn't exist is a silent -ENOENT (evidence: the current dir.c:1724-1752 has no WARN on !kn). I should be honest: I can't cite a single one-line fix commit; the fix is the rework + the kernfs WARN change, all present in this tree.\n\nAlso worth mentioning: if the user has to patch a 6.17-based OEM kernel, the minimal backport is:\n1. Change the WARN in `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns` to dev_dbg/no WARN on missing-children (upstream commit — Greg KH's \"kernfs: remove the WARN() in kernfs_remove_by_name_ns()\". I *think* it's part of his 2025 \"sysfs/kernfs fixes\" series, but — I won't assert a hash).\n2. And/or add a try-remove (ignore ENOENT) to the typec class.\n\nI'll present a \"recommended minimal backport\" based on the semantics of the code I have.\n\nAnother verification: in the current tree, is `partner->registered` gone? Search for \"registered\" in class.c? Quickly: search pattern \"registered\" — too many hits. Skip.\n\nAlso let me quickly confirm the caller of ucsi_unregister (2115-2162), and check the ordering there to cite: ucsi_unregister → first destroys workqueues? Let me fetch it — it's small, and it will show the current unplug-ordering fix.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me verify the current UCSI teardown ordering (`ucsi_unregister`) as the final piece of evidence."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2hm578mz","name":"codebase_memory","arguments":{"tool":"get_code_snippet","arguments":"{\"project\": \"workspace-linux\", \"qualified_name\": \"workspace-linux.drivers.usb.typec.ucsi.ucsi.ucsi_unregister\"}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.8:27b-q8_0","usage":{"input":49829,"output":3131,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTok