h of `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns()` (6.17 `fs/kernfs/dir.c:1706`), and (b) make the legacy `typec_unregister_partner()` tolerant of the `\"typec\"` directory already being gone (treat the `-ENOENT` from `kernfs_remove_by_name_ns()` as success). That both eliminates the splat and matches the fixed upstream semantics.\n- **Hardware note:** Dell should also consider a UCSI controller/BIOS fix, since the trigger is the controller emitting a stale CONNECT_CHANGE disconnect event at boot."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.8:27b-q8_0","usage":{"input":53686,"output":3059,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":56745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787748334247,"responseId":"chatcmpl-15","rawStopReason":"stop"},"toolResults":[]}
